{"_id":"694911863eeddc26d7c2ca82","roadmapSlug":"frontend","nodeId":"66ya3WdtlkjQyBTc3Lein","description":"# Service Workers\n\nService Workers are JavaScript files that act as proxy servers between web browsers and web servers. They can intercept network requests, cache resources, and deliver push notifications, even when the user is offline. This allows for improved performance and offline capabilities for web applications.","resources":[{"type":"article","title":"Service Worker API","url":"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/Service_Worker_API","_id":"6a686a7033d15c8310860a1a"},{"type":"article","title":"Service workers","url":"https://web.dev/learn/pwa/service-workers","_id":"6a686a7033d15c8310860a1b"},{"type":"article","title":"Service worker overview - Chrome","url":"https://developer.chrome.com/docs/workbox/service-worker-overview","_id":"6a686a7033d15c8310860a1c"},{"type":"video","title":"What is a service workers","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=A6MHtKkA0CA","_id":"6a686a7033d15c8310860a1d"}],"createdAt":"2025-12-22T09:38:14.618Z","updatedAt":"2026-07-28T08:38:08.225Z","lessonPacks":[],"paidResources":[],"contribution":"https://github.com/kamranahmedse/developer-roadmap/tree/master/roadmaps/frontend/content/66ya3WdtlkjQyBTc3Lein.md"}
